# verifier.py   (primes 397 199, 80 V14 points per prime)
CHECK charmult_exact PASS EXACT (ATLAS L2(11), rational arithmetic): dim Sym^d(10') = [1, 10, 55, 220, 715, 2002]; dim Hom_G(Sym^d(M*), 5) = dim Hom_G(Sym^d(M*), 5bar) = [0, 0, 1, 2, 7, 18] for d = 0..5; trivial multiplicity [1, 0, 1, 2, 4, 8].  The two 5-slots ALWAYS agree because chi_{Sym^d M} is rational and the slots are complex conjugates, so no symmetric power of M can separate them
CHECK model_397 PASS gauss^2=-11 True, S6^2=-I True, |<T6,S6>|=1320, projective-order profile [(1, 2), (2, 110), (3, 220), (5, 528), (6, 220), (11, 240)]
CHECK summands_397 PASS rank(10'-projector)=10, dim Ann(M) in Lambda^4 U=5, M and A are G-stable: True
CHECK v14points_397 PASS 80 distinct V14 points: all in M, all decomposable, all satisfy the 15 wedge-square (Plucker) equations (0 failures)
CHECK koszul_397 PASS equivariant Koszul complex of the 5 linear forms A on R(Gr(2,U)) = (+) S_{(d,d)}(U*): Hilbert function agrees mod p with the classical anticanonical h^0(-dK) = (7/6)d(d+1)(2d+1) + 2d+1 = [1, 10, 40, 105, 219, 396] of a genus-8 prime Fano threefold (True); n'(A) = [0, 0, 0, 1, 2, 3], n'(A^dual) = [0, 0, 1, 0, 2, 3] for d = 0..5  (n' = dim of the space of degree-d equivariant 5-tuples of forms ON V14)
CHECK invcubic_397 PASS trivial multiplicity in Sym^3(A) = 1 and in Sym^3(A^dual) = 1, so each 5-slot carries exactly ONE invariant cubic up to scale; the one on A equals 198 * Pf6 on 24/25 random points (sealed Klein identification X = {Pf = 0}), and the one on A^dual is therefore the conjugate Klein cubic
CHECK m2_v14ideal_397 PASS Macaulay2 on the 15 restricted Plucker quadrics in P^9: codim 6 / dim 4 / degree 14 / mingens 15 / hf {1, 10, 40, 105, 219, 396, 650} (3-fold of degree 14, minimally generated by the 15 quadrics, and the Hilbert function the Koszul complex predicts)
CHECK cov_A_d2_397 PASS Sym^2(M*) -> A: built 1 independent covariants by averaging 1 seeds over the 60 cosets of <T>; exact character multiplicity 1; equivariant for both generators at 16 random points; each nonzero on P(M)
CHECK kernel_A_d2_397 PASS evaluation at 80 V14 points has rank 0 (= the Koszul prediction n' = 0), so dim{F : F(sample) = 0} = 1; and 1 INDEPENDENT covariants were built from seeds lying in the ideal generated by the restricted Plucker quadrics -- these vanish identically on V14 -- so {F : F(sample) = 0} = {F : F|_V14 = 0} exactly, with no density assumption on the sample
CHECK land_A_d2_397 PASS EVERY degree-2 covariant into A vanishes identically on V14: the whole space is the Plucker-ideal kernel, so no degree-2 covariant defines any rational map V14 --> P(A) at all
CHECK cov_Adual_d2_397 PASS Sym^2(M*) -> Adual: built 1 independent covariants by averaging 1 seeds over the 60 cosets of <T>; exact character multiplicity 1; equivariant for both generators at 16 random points; each nonzero on P(M)
CHECK kernel_Adual_d2_397 PASS evaluation at 80 V14 points has rank 1 (= the Koszul prediction n' = 1), so dim{F : F(sample) = 0} = 0; and 0 INDEPENDENT covariants were built from seeds lying in the ideal generated by the restricted Plucker quadrics -- these vanish identically on V14 -- so {F : F(sample) = 0} = {F : F|_V14 = 0} exactly, with no density assumption on the sample
CHECK land_Adual_d2_397 PASS the restriction to V14 is unique up to scale, and the conjugate Klein cubic Pf6bar is nonzero at 80/80 image points, so the degree-2 map V14 --> P(Adual) misses the cubic
